("Which lab result is most useful when a CT pulmonary angiogram is being considered for suspected embolism?",
 "D-dimer", ["Hemoglobin A1c", "Serum amylase", "Lipid panel"],
 "A normal D-dimer makes a pulmonary embolism unlikely in a low-risk patient, so it often decides whether a CTPA is needed. HbA1c, amylase and lipids do not bear on clot."),
